Z||000005||Bill Osmer||12-24-2001||07:55 PM||||Because they're BOTH not working, try reversing one of the LEDs wiring polarity. You're right in thinking that they never burn out, especially in pairs. Usually, they're wired backwards.<P>IMHP<P>B<P>------------------<BR>Bill Osmer<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forumcardsig2.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000006||Alex2004||12-24-2001||09:31 PM||||Well i just messed w/ the LED and reversed the polarity and it's still  isn't working.  the driver's switch is but passenger is not. i checked everything on the led. ground...hot, changed both and it still isn't working but it did work when i tested it.  hmm....maybe i accidently fried the chip for the led whenever a few wires touched?!?... hmm....i guess i'll go buy another switch from the slavage yard.  any other ideas or fixes of what might be wrong?  let me know... thanks...alex...<P>ps..only one of them doens't work..the other does...||||reg||13
Z||000007||Bill Osmer||12-26-2001||03:48 PM||||Such a puzzlement!!!<P>Have you tried using the wires to the switch that works??<P> It'd be a shame that you'd have to get another switch. I've not had the opportunity to try a repair of the LED, although I think it would be possible. If you've tried everything, you could send it to me and I'd try a repair or two, then return it.<P>LMK<P>Bill||||reg||5
